+# Power features: Now and next, Catch up, smarter quick add, weekly review reminder
+
+Plain text for the Help sheet and README (merge by hand).
+
+## Now and next (`#now-next`)
+- **Now and next** (card on Today, tile in All tools, palette "Now and next" or "what should I do now", or the link `#now-next`): your day as one strip from 7am to 11pm (wider when you have earlier or later plans). Events and shifts in their own colors, grey stripes for travel to and from work, green for free time and a red line for now. Tap a block to open it.
+- One line says where you are: "Free now until 1pm · 3h, then Dentist at 1pm", or "Now: Outback until 10pm · next free 10:20pm".
+- **Do next** shows the 2 tasks that best fit the free time you have (**More** opens the full sheet with 5): high priority, overdue and due today first, and tasks that fit the gap before ones that do not (a task with no time estimate counts as 30 minutes). Each says why ("high priority · 2 days late · 45m · Kalshi bot"). Ideas and tasks dated later are left out.
+- On each task: the box marks it done (a repeating task puts its next one on the calendar, Undo is offered), the title opens the task, the clock starts the focus timer, and the cross hides it for 3 hours ("Not now", kept on this phone only).
+- Late in the evening the card shows tomorrow instead: "Day is done. Tomorrow starts with Electric at 7am."
+
+## Catch up (`#catch-up`)
+- When 2 or more tasks are overdue, a one-line **Catch up** card sits in Needs you now ("4 overdue tasks, the oldest 6 days late", button **Spread them**). It is also in All tools, the palette ("catch up") and the link `#catch-up`.
+- **Spread smart** places them highest priority and oldest first, each on the first of the next 7 days with room. Room is 60% of that day's free time between 7am and 10pm after shifts, events and travel, minus the tasks already planned that day, and at most 3 catch-up tasks a day. A task that does not fit anywhere is left as it is.
+- Or move them all to today, all to tomorrow, or take the date off (No date). Every task has its own picker: any of the next 7 days, No date, Mark done (not offered for repeating tasks) or Leave as is.
+- Nothing changes until **Apply**. The toast says what happened ("Caught up: 3 moved, 1 done") and **Undo** puts every task back.
+
+## Smarter quick add (Quick capture and the Today quick add box)
+- Several days at once: "gym tue thu 7am" adds a weekly event on Tuesday and Thursday. "every other tue 3pm", "yoga tuesdays 6pm" and "gym weekends 9am" work too. Without a time ("water plants mon thu") you get weekly tasks.
+- A time range or a length: "Outback fri 4-10pm", "electric 7-3:30", "standup 9:30-10 tomorrow", "study for 90 min thu 6pm", "deep work 2h tomorrow" (a task with a 2 h estimate). "noon" works as a time.
+- A title that names one of your jobs makes it that job's shift: "Outback fri 4-10pm" adds an Outback Steakhouse shift (so Hours, Earnings, Payday and travel count it). Every other event gets your last used type, but never a job's type, so a gym block can never count as work (the same rule as Find a time).
+- More dates: "nov 15", "5th of december", "on the 5th", "next week" (Monday), "this weekend", "end of month", "end of week", "in 2 weeks", "in a month", plus "monthly", "every other week" and "yearly" repeats.
+- Money due: "pay MFFU 91.80 on the 5th" becomes the task "Pay MFFU $91.80" on the 5th, with a one-tap **Monthly bill on the 5th** instead. "car insurance 180 due the 20th" works the same way. With a repeat it becomes a bill straight away: "netflix 15.49 monthly on the 12th", "rent 1200 on the 1st every month", "pay gym 30 every week fri". Bills go into Bills and the calendar like the ones you add there.
+- The preview always says what will be added before you press Add. Everything the app already understood is unchanged: "call Sam fri 3pm #nq", "gym tomorrow 7am", "paid $40 gas", "got 85 tips", "water 24", "ate 2 eggs", "note: ...", "idea: ..." go to the same place as before. "pay $40 gas" is still money spent today. If the guess is wrong, **Change** hands the sentence back to the normal reader.
+
+## Weekly review reminder
+- From Friday 3pm to Monday night a one-line **Weekly review** card sits on Today until that week's review is written ("Nov 1 to 7 · 2 weeks in a row. Wins, fixes and next week's top 3, in 3 minutes"). **Start** opens the Review page on the right week (the one holding the most recent Friday). Writing anything in it (a win, a fix, a priority, or creating the priority tasks) counts as done, and the card goes away.
+- The run of weeks in a row counts back from that week (or from the week before, while this one is still open), so the streak is never lost before Monday is over.
+
+## Notes for the lead (not for the Help sheet)
+- Code: `planner/ext-power.js`, loaded by one `<script src="ext-power.js">` in `<head>`. It waits for the `planner:ready` event fired by the **EXT API** block in `index.html` (`window.PlannerAPI`: the app's own helpers, read-only access to `S` through a getter). Nothing else in `index.html` changed.
+- Data: no new synced collection and no new field in `planner.v1`. Changes to tasks, events and bills go through `commit()` after `snapshot()`, exactly like the app's own sheets (sync stamps, tombstones and Undo all work). The only new key is the device-only `planner.power.skip` ({ task id: hidden until ms }).
+- Today cards `pwnow` (tier Today, above Schedule), `pwreview` (tier Today, Friday 3pm to Monday only) and `pwcatch` (tier Needs you now, soft label "Overdue", so the "N things need you" count is unchanged) are added to `TO_CARDS`, so Customize Today can hide and move them. Tiles `pwnow` and `pwcatch` (group Calendar) in `HB_TOOLS`, commands `px-now` and `px-catch` in `PK_CMDS`.
+- Pure helpers on `window.__pw`: `review(today)` ({ ws, done, streak }), `parse(text, today)` (null = left to the app's `qcParse` / `addTask`), `label`, `spread(tasks, days, perDay)`, `pick(tasks, { today, minutes, skip, now })`, `day(key, nowMin)`, `caps(today, n)`, `rangeOf(text)`.
+- The claude.ai copy built by `build_hosted.py` does not load the file unless `ext-power.js` is published next to the page; without it the app runs exactly as before.
+- Tests: `planner/tests/power.test.js` (PORT env, default 8790).
